
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:mentions@

%9Parameters:%9

    CLEAR:       Removes the entries from the Mentions window (as
                 /SCROLLBACK CLEAR does); the log file is not touched.

    Without an argument (or with any other one) goes to the Mentions
    window.

%9Description:%9

    Goes to the Mentions window, where erssi collects what was written to
    you: private messages and private /ME actions, NOTICEs from people to
    your nick (not from servers, not sent to a channel or a server mask),
    DCC CHAT messages and channel hilights. Messages that /IGNORE hides
    are left out, and so are those from a nick with a NOHILIGHT ignore
    (/IGNORE nick MSGS NOHILIGHT).

    A channel hilight is a channel message or /ME action that erssi shows
    as a hilight: your nick in it (hilight_nick_matches, and
    hilight_nick_matches_everywhere for the nick anywhere in the line) or
    a match of a /HILIGHT rule (an action with your nick is a hilight
    only through a rule, e.g. /HILIGHT -level ACTIONS yournick). It is
    recorded with the sender's whole nick and the text as it was sent,
    not as the theme shows it. Your own lines are never hilights. A
    hilight that a script prints into a channel is recorded with the
    nick "?" and the printed line, unless it is printed while that
    channel's message is shown: then it counts as that message and is
    recorded with its sender.

    Entries have the HILIGHT level, so the window gets the hilight colour
    in the window list.

    The window is created in the background at startup and has
    /WINDOW IMMORTAL on. If it is closed anyway (after
    /WINDOW IMMORTAL OFF), it is created again.

    With mentions_log on, every entry is also appended to a log file in
    the form "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS [tag] place <nick> text", so it survives
    a restart. The file is created with mode 0600 and a missing directory
    with mode 0700. Control characters in the text are written as spaces.

    Networks named in mentions_exclude_networks are left out, both from the
    window and from the log (for example a Bitlbee gateway). This
    includes DCC CHATs that were offered through such a network.

%9Settings:%9

    mentions_window = Mentions
        Name of the Mentions window. Empty: no window; the log and the
        "mention" signal still work. A name another window already has
        is refused.
    mentions_log = OFF
        Append every entry to the log file.
    mentions_log_file =
        The log file. Empty means logs/mentions.log in the irssi
        directory; '~' is your home directory; a relative name is in
        the irssi directory.
    mentions_exclude_networks =
        Networks (chat network names, separated by spaces or commas)
        whose messages are not mentions.

%9Examples:%9

    /MENTIONS
    /MENTIONS CLEAR
    /SET mentions_log ON
    /SET mentions_exclude_networks Bitlbee

%9See also:%9 HILIGHT, IGNORE, LASTLOG, SCROLLBACK, WINDOW

